# Cloudflare Pages redirects
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
#
# Order matters: the FIRST matching rule wins, and Cloudflare does not chain
# redirects. Any specific `/es/...` rule must therefore appear before the
# `/es/*` catch-all at the bottom AND point straight at its final URL.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Language swap: Spanish moved from /es to the site root
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Spanish is the community's primary language and is now served at `/`, with
# English under `/en`. Every previously published `/es/...` URL keeps working
# via a permanent redirect to its new root URL.
#
# Note: the old English URLs (`/about`, `/blog/...`) cannot be redirected to
# `/en/...` — those paths now legitimately serve Spanish. English content is
# re-announced through the updated sitemap and hreflang tags instead.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# cabuya.org migration — retired route families from the previous site
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The site became cabuya.org. These route families no longer exist; each is sent
# to the closest surviving page rather than 404ing, because external links and
# search indexes still point at them.
#
# Route slugs are English in both languages; Spanish is served unprefixed.
# Only retired paths appear here — a live page must never be listed, or the
# redirect shadows the page itself.
#
# Ordered most-specific first. These MUST appear before the `/es/*` catch-all.

